# TRUE POSITIVE, remediated in the working tree and neutralised at the source.
# These two are NOT false positives and must not be read as such.
#
# Commit c7846dc committed a live single-use bootstrap enrolment token into
# docs/evidence/phase-0/wp0.2-summary.md (P0-10, gate §2.8). It is redacted at
# HEAD. These entries exist only because the value is still reachable in history.
#
# Why a fingerprint rather than a rewrite: `git filter-repo` is not installed on
# this machine, and rewriting 31 commits with `filter-branch` to scrub a token
# that is already dead is a worse trade than recording why it is dead. There is
# no remote — nothing has ever been pushed — so the history is local and can
# still be rewritten cheaply if `filter-repo` is installed before first push.
# That is the preferred endgame and is tracked in
# docs/evidence/phase-0/gate-remediation-api.md.
#
# Why the token is dead, not merely expired: it was single-use, minted against
# the scratch database `personalfi_wp02` on the dev Postgres, and it was never
# redeemed (`registration_tokens.used_at IS NULL`, one row, expiring
# 2026-09-12T18:42:07Z). That database was dropped WITH (FORCE) and recreated
# empty during this remediation, so the row the token would have been validated
# against no longer exists in any database anywhere. It never reached a
# deployment, and it authenticated nothing beyond a throwaway local enrolment.
c7846dc6282f6ae7156e56b36f47a8de14d969aa:docs/evidence/phase-0/wp0.2-summary.md:generic-api-key:96
